ROADMAP.md:109:   6. Ghost permissions for trusted code.
ROADMAP.md:157:| A. Core and theorem | Dispose of the spec audit. The owner decides the whole Core shape before implementation, in four stages: provisional approval (A2a), a proposed `Spec.lean` with four checked design theorems (A2b), integration of its parts with their interaction proofs, the modular layout and the browsable owner view (A2i), and the owner's freeze of the integrated scopes (A2c). State the semantic contract and the end-to-end theorem in Lean, and list the trusted base. | Core frozen by the owner after the four design theorems and the integration proofs are kernel-checked. The theorem, its holes and the trusted base on main. |
ROADMAP.md:179:| A3 | State the theorem and the trusted base in Lean | R-0502, R-0506, R-0508, R-0509, R-0500, R-0588 | The contract and the modular layout from A2i are on main. The theorem, with its holes, the named values-to-bytes boundary and the trusted-base inventory, is on main. The theorem skeleton uses concrete slice interfaces; its semantic-premise inventory is separate from the axiom audit. Before slice 0's authoritative claim, its actual Core fragment is connected to the frozen definitions and any instrumentation erasure it uses is proved; later features require integration proofs into that same Core. Slice 0 starts after A2c and the applicable A3 foundations for its authoritative claims; a provisional skeleton may start earlier and claims nothing normative. |
ROADMAP.md:180:| B0 | Build and qualify slice 0, the proof spine ([decision](docs/decisions.md#decided-project-proof-infrastructure)) | R-0501, R-0581, R-0580, R-0583, R-0503, R-0578, R-0579, R-0425, R-0499, R-0493, R-0507, R-0521, R-0552, R-0118, R-0498, R-0553, R-0573, R-0575, R-0585, R-0588, R-0593, R-0594, R-0577, R-0272, R-0301, R-0550 | Slice 0 runs through every used IR to two unverified native builds, LLVM and the LCB, whose full observations CI compares with each other and with the expected outcome, with per-lowering proofs, independent supported-subset coverage, the composed conditional image theorem, artifact binding, example correctness, including transport to the exact native artifact under the named premises, and classified differential and refusal controls. The per-function facts report (R-0575) is produced for every slice-0 function, each fact and obligation with its source location. The BIR → LCB-IR adapter proof (R-0579) is the first backend proof. Reproducible builds, final-artifact stack facts, the trusted-base statement, the front-end differential fuzzer, ASan/UBSan runs, binary-size tracking and the frozen, versioned JSON schema start here. This does not trigger legacy deletion. |
ROADMAP.md:203:scheduled: `free` (OD59), `trusted mod` (OD61), mutable global cells (OD8), `process_exit` (OD136),
ROADMAP.md:209:| 0 | `main -> u8`, immutable typed `u8` lets, decimal literals (leading zero refused), reads, parentheses, checked `+`, return; `concrete build` and `concrete facts`; the diagnostics record; both backends; reproducible builds; each program's maximum stack use, measured from the final binary on both backends, with the `Concrete.toml` stack budget; the trusted-base statement in facts; the random-program differential fuzzer; AddressSanitizer and UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer; binary-size tracking; the frozen, versioned JSON schema for diagnostics and facts from the first front-end output | B0 |
